    "answer": {
      "short": "$111.7\\text{ cm}$",
      "worked": "Each angle is $60^\\circ$. Let the side length be $s$ cm.\n$$\\begin{align*}600&=\\frac12s^2\\sin60^\\circ\\\\s^2&=\\frac{1200}{\\sin60^\\circ}\\\\s&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1200}{\\sin60^\\circ}}\\\\P&=3\\sqrt{\\frac{1200}{\\sin60^\\circ}}\\\\P&\\approx111.7\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
